    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40595" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rē^clīnātōrĭum</span></b> ,
			i, n.
		reclino; in plur., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the back of a couch</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">reclinatoria vulgus appellat ornamenta
					lectorum, quae fulciunt toros sive caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 19, 26, 3</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The seat in a chariot</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aureum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Cant. 3, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
